#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059422 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/id #uuid "e95210c5-adb4-519e-bbec-e240dac32fd8" :question/math-academy-id "e-3614" :question/problem "Write $2\\sin{15^\\circ} \\cos{15^\\circ}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=15^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\sin 15^{∘}\\cos 15^{∘} &= \\sin (2 \\cdot 15^{∘}) = \\sin 30^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059423 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/id #uuid "35535b08-b3d8-5037-a821-6815577169d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-3618" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)}$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\frac{1}{2}[2\\sin (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{24})]\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\n$$\n\nwe can further simplify the above expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[2\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12})] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[\\sin (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{12})] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}\\sin (\\frac{π}{6}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)} = \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059424 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/id #uuid "b03496ac-c3b2-5d65-a3e3-2a33ea0cb862" :question/math-academy-id "e-3619" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{\\sin 25^\\circ}{\\sin 50^\\circ}$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=25^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left(2\\cdot 25^\\circ\\right) = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\sin 50^\\circ = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the ${\\color{blue} \\sin 50^\\circ}$ in the denominator as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{\\sin 50^{∘}} &= \\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{2\\sin 25^{∘}\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{2\\sin 25^{∘}\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\sec 25^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059425 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "539b5b86-7b31-52c9-be04-e80d6799b68a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3623" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $3\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac {\\pi}{8}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\sin (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{8}) \\\\\n&= \\sin (\\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2\\sin \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 1 2\n$$\n\ngives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3 \\, {\\color{black}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}} = 3 \\left(\\color{black} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\right) = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4483a191-ab5f-53cc-9a25-631101495ec5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256212} {:answer/id #uuid "1bca9c9f-347e-50cd-983a-012520b04ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256213} {:answer/id #uuid "7182fa70-cf00-5a72-8698-deb11fabc8da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256214} {:answer/id #uuid "be86f2e5-0b3d-52c0-a00f-2a4b04f18b34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256215} {:answer/id #uuid "4b12d860-258e-5359-827c-56ef56e1e69d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be86f2e5-0b3d-52c0-a00f-2a4b04f18b34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256215} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4715576-2b79-520b-9527-45c19ddc2f36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9834bdc8-d968-5825-adae-a20e0fb4ec63" :question/math-academy-id "q-119948" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ into the above, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{10}) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9fa087f-f6db-5d41-bce6-176e0dfc84bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265643} {:answer/id #uuid "8291aef2-a55a-5035-960c-b2fd32db51b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265644} {:answer/id #uuid "74e0f6fd-d7a9-5e32-b935-3d2d63d15eee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265645} {:answer/id #uuid "16abd149-1622-5870-acac-08550572af4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265646} {:answer/id #uuid "0d7a1573-25a2-57b7-9e53-7a5153bbcccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d7a1573-25a2-57b7-9e53-7a5153bbcccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265647} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e71bada-abf2-5012-a4dd-26de4973c091" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d2067af-e1b2-5f04-ba26-5b2307cb8aa1" :question/math-academy-id "q-120017" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}).\n$$\n\nRewriting the given expression using the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281682 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "299a4036-7401-5ec0-be7f-2022c81d1096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281684} {:answer/id #uuid "5e74f45f-6145-5c80-9cfe-c0ed118e55bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281685} {:answer/id #uuid "9d36f77e-f34f-5865-a379-4b6195857bef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281686} {:answer/id #uuid "023f9a63-2f22-5145-94fb-5736a13bae5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281687} {:answer/id #uuid "a1cb1f7d-bc36-5ff9-a3ee-57d48f84ac6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e74f45f-6145-5c80-9cfe-c0ed118e55bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281685} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac5edacb-bfbd-58aa-8234-65a8e4b4cad7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "178fb81d-b009-5067-9e70-c3ccaf69f0be" :question/math-academy-id "q-120029" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{100}^{∘}\\operatorname{tan}⁡{50}^{∘}}{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={50}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {50}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡({100}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{100}^{∘}\\operatorname{tan}⁡{50}^{∘}}{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}}{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing  the Pythagorean identity ${sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}=1-{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} & =\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})}{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}} \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186257401 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ecfd948-ebcb-56b9-8393-d73b7b5edf38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270442} {:answer/id #uuid "e88aabae-de3a-56f7-970d-942816d9d158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3)/(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270443} {:answer/id #uuid "ee141aa1-9b0f-5121-bbb4-ca3e629d2447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270444} {:answer/id #uuid "5669b4ae-d738-5b7f-945b-508dddefea1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1)/(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270445} {:answer/id #uuid "df61159e-1675-59bb-9637-8070393a178f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df61159e-1675-59bb-9637-8070393a178f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270446} :answer-field/id #uuid "252e3e40-9b54-5a12-85ce-a632bc29687a" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72bde4a1-d04b-50b4-bd0e-183a00744709" :question/math-academy-id "q-120087" :question/problem "$10\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}({150}^{∘})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x=\\operatorname{sin}2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={75}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}(2\\cdot {75}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}({150}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}({150}^{∘}) & =5\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘})]\\operatorname{csc}({150}^{∘}) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}({150}^{∘})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}({150}^{∘})} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed202dc5-ee81-586d-86e5-9ab11f560c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡({70}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281691} {:answer/id #uuid "28acbdae-db5d-555e-9992-ecf841025666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡({70}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281692} {:answer/id #uuid "397beb83-55b4-5c02-b7ad-41cdd0598e99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281693} {:answer/id #uuid "66ebe9bc-0c6a-5192-a142-6bafb0f428aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281694} {:answer/id #uuid "c14d2ba0-9102-545b-b898-0f3bfdac943f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "397beb83-55b4-5c02-b7ad-41cdd0598e99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281693} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe430471-858f-5d77-bff2-394ae8b417ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4169dfb7-ab66-5202-bba3-44ee807d3294" :question/math-academy-id "q-120088" :question/problem "$4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={70}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {70}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘}) & =2\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})]\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060162 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ac8d37f-1f11-5095-87c7-37fd160497dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :a